For more up-to-date installation guide, please check the web-site:
http://lyntin.sourceforge.net


Unix/Linux 
1. make sure you have Python 1.5.2 and Tcl/Tk 8.0 (you need Tcl/Tk 
   only to use the GUI--otherwise you can still use the console textui) 
   installed 
2. download the version you're looking for (below) 
3. untar the client into ~/lyntin
4. create a LYNTINDIR environment variable set to the lyntin directory 
   or alternately start lyntin from the lyntin directory (version 1.3.1 
   and up) 
5. change the permissions on lt or lt-gui.py or lt-text.py (depending on 
   which one you plan on using to run lyntin) so that it's executable and 
   fix the first line in it so that it correctly points to your python 
   executable 
6. then run:
      lyntin.py [file]
      lyntin.py -tk [file]

   he gui one will only work if you've got Tcl/Tk installed. 

Windows 
1. make sure you have Python 1.5.2 and Tcl/Tk 8.0 (you need Tcl/Tk only 
   to use the GUI--otherwise you can still use the console textui) installed 
2. download the version you're looking for (below) 
3. unzip the client into c:\lyntin 
4. create a shortcut on your desktop: 
      Target: [path you put it in]\lyntin.py -tk 
      Start in: [path you put it in] 
5. double-click on the shortcut to run Lyntin



After that, we have in-game help which you can access via #help.  If you
are really new to Lyntin, read README then read #help general.
